  "chapter": 453,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 12 Chapter 453\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8596-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the education law, in relation to expanding eligi-\n        bility under the veterans tuition awards program\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would expand the number of  military  veterans  eligible  to\nreceive  Veterans  Tuition  Awards.  The Veterans Tuition Awards program\nprovides awards covering the cost of college tuition for eligible  mili-\ntary veterans in New York. The awards are equal to the amount of tuition\ncharged  at  SUNY  institutions  and  are  in addition to those benefits\nprovided under the federal GI Bill and Pell grant program.    Currently,\nonly veterans having served in combat after 1961 and those having served\nin  the  Vietnam, Persian Gulf, or Afghanistan conflicts are eligible to\nreceive Veterans Tuition Awards.\n \n  I am proud to sign this bill into law. Expanding these awards to  more\nof  our veterans is a vitally important action. However, the bill passed\nby the Legislature required various changes before it could  be  signed.\nThese include clarifying the scope of eligibility for active duty veter-\nans and the calculation of award amounts.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to make these changes\nin  the next legislative session. These changes will ensure the Veterans\nTuition Awards benefit is available to all military  veterans  who  have\nserved at least four years on active duty. Based on that agreement, I am\nplease to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2024
 },
